# Svelte and SvelteKit Conventions

## Svelte 5 Features
- Use runes (`$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`) for reactivity
- Use `$derived` for computed values
- Implement `$effect` for side effects
- Keep components small and focused

## SvelteKit 2 Patterns
- Use server-side data loading in `+page.server.ts` files
- Implement form actions in `+page.server.ts` for POST/PUT/DELETE operations
- Use page data with `+page.ts` for client-side loading
- Implement error handling with `+error.svelte` pages
- Use layout groups for shared layouts

## Routing
- Place routes in [src/routes](mdc:src/routes)
- Use `+page.svelte` for page components
- Implement layouts with `+layout.svelte`
- Handle loading states with `+loading.svelte`
- Use route parameters with `[param]` syntax

## State Management
- Use reactive classes in `svelte.ts` files for global state
- Implement local state with runes
- Use URL state for shareable data
- Leverage form actions for server mutations

- Use `+server.ts` for API endpoints
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Use streaming for large data sets
- Optimize assets with static adapter
- Implement proper preloading
